          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Su-Schrieffer-Heeger model
            (SSH) is a simple
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+chain"} spin chain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            for a type of 1-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+material"} quantum material
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theoretical+physics"} theoretical physics
            it mainly serves as an instructive toy model example of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron+band"} electron band
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#SuSchriefferHeeger79"} Su, Schrieffer &amp; Heeger 1979
          %p
            As a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+model"} lattice model
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron+band"} band
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}_n \simeq \mathbb{C}^2 \simeq \mathbb{C}\langle A, B\rangle
            at each site, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+operator"} Hamiltonian operator
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            of
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                an
                %em intracell
                hopping term between sites
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                in the same cell
            %li
              %p
                an
                %em extracell
                hopping term between the
                = succeed "-site" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                = succeed "-site" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The parameter space of the model is that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            of these two terms:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}
                , the intracell hopping strength,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \in \mathbb{R}_{\gt 0}
                , the intercell hopping strength.
          %p
            After
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+Hamiltonian"} Bloch Hamiltonian
            of the SSH model
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H =
                  \\textstyle{\int_{[k] \in S^1}} H_{k}
                  \\;\in\;
                  End\Big(
                  \\textstyle{\int_{k \in S^1}} \mathbb{C}^2
                  \\Big)
          %p
            is given (up to arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            shift and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+transformation"} unitary transformation
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AsbóthOroszlányPályi16"} Asbóth, Oroszlány &amp; Pályi 2016 (1.18)
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#BatraSheet20"} Batra &amp; Sheet 2020
          #eq:TheBlochHamiltonian.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi v
                          %mo +
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi cos
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi sin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mi y
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  [k]
                  \&amp;\mapsto
                  H_{[k]}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;\coloneqq
                  \\big(
                  v + w \cdot cos(k)
                  \\big)
                  \\sigma_x
                  +
                  \\big(
                  w \cdot sin(k)
                  \\big)
                  \\sigma_y
                  \\,,
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{(-)} \in End(\mathbb{C}^2)
            denotes the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+matrices"} Pauli matrices
          %p
            To note here that these Bloch Hamiltonians
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{[k]}
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheBlochHamiltonian"} (1)
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                have no contribution of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+matrix"} Pauli matrix
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_z
              #eq:ChiralSymmetry.maruku-equation
                %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi z
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi z
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\sigma_z H_{[k]} \sigma_z = - H_{[k]}
                      \\,,
            %li
              %p
                generically have two
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
                of opposite sign (labeling the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+band"} valence band
                of negative energy and the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conduction+band"} conduction band
                of positive energy, respectively), except when
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{[k]} = 0
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+gap"} energy gap
                between these eigenvalues closes, which happens when
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo =
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = w
          %p
            Hence for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = w
            the SSH model describes an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conductor"} conductor
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \neq w
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/insulator"} insulator
          %p
            In the latter case there are still two qualitatively different regimes: When
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \lt w
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bloch+Hamiltonian"} Bloch Hamiltonian
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheBlochHamiltonian"} (1)
            regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/map"} map
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of
            %em gapped
            and
            %em chiral
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChiralSymmetry"} (2)
            2-band Hamiltonians
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi End
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mn 2
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mi gap
                              %mo ,
                              %mi chr
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mi H
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi End
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℂ
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo{:maxsize => "2.4em", :minsize => "2.4em"} |
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtable{:columnalign => "center", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %msup
                                      %mi H
                                      %mo †
                                    %mo =
                                    %mi H
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %msub
                                      %mi σ
                                      %mi z
                                    %mi H
                                    %msub
                                      %mi σ
                                      %mi z
                                    %mo =
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mi H
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %msub
                                      %mi Eig
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo &gt;
                                        %mn 0
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi H
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ≃
                                    %mi ℂ
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                    %msub
                                      %mi Eig
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo &lt;
                                        %mn 0
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi H
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo ≃
                                    %mi ℂ
                            %mo }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ∖
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi hmpty
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  H_{(-)}
                  \\colon
                  S^1
                  \&amp;
                  \\longrightarrow
                  End(\mathbb{C}^2)_{gap, chr}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\left\{
                  H \in End(\mathbb{C}^2)
                  \\,\bigg\vert\,
                  \\substack{
                  H^\dagger = H,\, \sigma_z H \sigma_z = - H
                  \\\
                  Eig_{\gt 0}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}
                  ,\,
                  Eig_{\lt 0}(H) \simeq \mathbb{C}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{R}^2 \setminus \{0\}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;
                  \\underset{hmpty}{\simeq}
                  S^1
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            has a non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+classification+of+topological+phases"} hence
            describes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phase+of+matter"} phase
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+degree"} Hopf degree
            (“winding number”) equal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
            (depending on conventions); while for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \gt w
            the Hopf degree winding number vanishes, which hence describes an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/insulator"} insulator
            phase.
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haldane+model"} Haldane model
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#SuSchriefferHeeger79
              W. P. Su, J. R. Schrieffer, A. J. Heeger:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Solitons in Polyacetylene
              %strong 42
              (1979) 1698 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.42.1698"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.42.1698
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "AsbóthOroszlányPályi16"}
              %p
                János K. Asbóth, László Oroszlány, András Pályi, Chapter 1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Short Course on Topological Insulators: Band-structure topology and edge states in one and two dimensions
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 919
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.02295"} arXiv:1509.02295
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-25607-8"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-25607-8
            %li#BatraSheet20
              %p
                Navketan Batra, Goutam Sheet:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Understanding Basic Concepts of Topological Insulators Through Su-Schrieffer-Heeger (SSH) Model
                %strong 25
                (2020) 765-786 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1906.08435"}> arXiv:1906.08435
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s12045-020-0995-x"} doi:10.1007/s12045-020-0995-x
            %li
              %p
                Weibo Xu:
                %em The Su-Schrieffer-Heeger model on a one-dimensional lattice: Analytical wave functions of topological edge states
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.16708"}> arXiv:2509.16708
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia:
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su%E2%80%93Schrieffer%E2%80%93Heeger_model"} Su–Schrieffer–Heeger model
        .revisedby
